            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Results of treatment of 36 patients aged from 25 to 72 years with ventricular extrasystole and paroxysms of atrial fibrillation demonstrated that the absence of contraindications combined treatment with antiarrhythmic drugs is justifiable provided a thorough medical control is performed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
